# Build and debug a component

**Never install built RPMs on your host** — they target the distro, not your dev
machine. Use isolated component tests or a chroot with the `azldev-mock` skill.
`azldev comp build` runs RPM build-time checks; `azldev component test <name>` runs
the separately configured artifact tests.

## Build

```sh
azldev comp build -p <name>                                     # one component
azldev comp build -p <a> -p <b> --local-repo-with-publish <dir> # chain deps via a local repo
azldev comp build -p <name> --local-repo <dir>                  # rebuild against a populated repo
```

Build foundational packages before their dependents. RPMs land in the project's
configured output directory (`out` by default). `-q` quiets output but hides build
progress — use it only for inner-loop builds you expect to succeed.

## The inner loop

investigate → modify → render → build → test → inspect

| Step | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Investigate | read the rendered spec under `{{ .RenderedSpecsDir }}/`, or `azldev comp diff-sources -p <name>` |
| Modify | edit the component's `.comp.toml` (see the `azldev-overlays` and `azldev-comp-toml` skills) |
| Verify | `azldev comp render -p <name>` (fast — skips source tarballs) |
| Build | `azldev comp build -p <name>` |
| Test | `azldev component test <name>` (or a mock shell for manual debugging) |
| Inspect | `azldev comp build -p <name> --preserve-buildenv always`, then a mock shell |

Prefer `comp render` for quick overlay verification; use `comp diff-sources` to see the
exact overlay effect (it fetches sources once, applies overlays to a copy, and diffs the
two trees). Builds can be slow — set generous timeouts.

Component tests reuse local RPMs, building when missing; `--rebuild` forces a
build. Supporting images default to named LKG images in the selected distro
version. Override with `--base-image`, `--base-image-path`, or
`--rebuild-base-image`; `--rpm` selects explicit candidates instead of the
complete component output. Mutually conflicting subpackages require an
explicit compatible subset for now. `--test` accepts test/group names.
TMT supports `--execution vm`, `container`, `ssh`, or `host`; host/SSH execution
may modify the target and must only be used on designated test systems.
LISA uses a VM; pytest inspects candidate files via `AZLDEV_TEST_INPUTS`.

Source overrides are copied into private runtimes, not edited in place.
TMT retains per-case results, `tmt-output.log`, and `python-environment.txt`
under the selected work directory; do not depend on temporary venv paths.
VM inputs may be RAW, qcow2, VHD, or VHDX; conversion never modifies the original.
Use TMT `context` for fmf adjustments and `cloud-init-runcmds` for guest VM hooks.
Bootstrap policy must be explicit: there are no automatic guest firewall or
`fedora` account workarounds. For session-mode testcloud with firewalld enabled,
configure the named image's `test-defaults.tmt` or the test's `tmt` settings to
permit SSH and TCP 10022 before readiness. Image defaults resolve from the
distro catalog, then explicit same-name project overrides, then per-test
overrides, independent of local/LKG artifact origin. Lists replace, and `[]`
disables inherited commands. An anonymous `--base-image-path` does not inherit
an image identity; add `--base-image NAME` to explicitly associate the file.
Native extra arguments are scope-checked and cannot override managed inputs.
TMT VM plans must have at most one provision phase. All-skipped runs are skipped;
reporting or cleanup failures remain errors even if tests also failed.
Every adapter reports normalized cases; collecting zero cases is an error.
Candidate files are snapshotted read-only per invocation; inspect `originalPath`
and `sha256` in the input manifest for provenance after snapshot cleanup.
Pytest `install=none` uses `{{ .WorkDir }}/pytest-venv/<test-name>` without installing dependencies.

Finalize with `azldev comp refresh-upstream-commit -p <name>` before opening a PR (see the
`azldev-refresh-upstream-commit` skill).

## Debugging build failures

1. **Render error mentioning a non-standard `Release` tag** — a release-calculation
   issue; see the `azldev-comp-toml` skill.
2. **Overlay did not apply as expected** — `azldev comp diff-sources -p <name>` shows
   what the overlays actually change.
3. **Inspect the build environment** — `azldev comp build -p <name> --preserve-buildenv
   on-failure` (values `on-failure`, `always`, `never`), then enter a mock shell.
4. **Failing `%check`** — fix the tests first (root cause, upstream patches, targeted
   fixes). Only as a last resort, disable with `build.check.skip = true` and a required
   `build.check.skip_reason` explaining what fails, why it cannot be fixed, and whether it
   is temporary. A transient `--no-check` build flag exists for one-off local builds.

Per-component build tweaks (`build.defines`, `build.without`) live in the `.comp.toml` —
see the `azldev-comp-toml` skill.

